Author:   thecozies
Added:    2021-12-30 (HackerSM64 commit f3e61a31)

These five 16x16 rgba16 glyphs are original community-drawn art that fills
the null J/Q/V/X/Z slots left by the vanilla US (and CN) HUD font -- they
are NOT extracted from any Nintendo ROM, and are used here specifically to
avoid the Nintendo-IP JP-ROM-ripped alternative. HackerSM64 ships no
LICENSE file; this NOTICE records the provenance and attributes the
original artist and source project, per HackerSM64's own stated intent as
a base for romhacks. If you are the artist/maintainers and want a
different attribution or removal, please open an issue.

Wired into the null `main_hud_lut` slots in bin/segment2.c (spec #75,
sub-issue #77): src/game/hud.c's render_hud_top_right_corner uses the
existing print_text HUD font path, and these glyphs are what make names
containing J/Q/V/X/Z render as real letters instead of garbage.
